# The capture manifest is an append-only ledger: rows are only ever added, and
# every row is keyed by URL with a timestamp. When two branches both capture,
# both append at the end of the file and git reports a conflict over a "both
# added lines here" hunk that has no actual disagreement in it.
#
# union tells git to keep both sides instead. Ordering between the two sets is
# not preserved and an identical row appended on both sides survives twice —
# both are harmless here, because the ledger is read as "last row per URL" and
# rows carry their own timestamps.
data/manifest/*.csv     merge=union

# Deliberately NOT union-merged: data/races.csv and data/coverage.csv are
# regenerated wholesale and sorted deterministically (build plan 3.3), so a
# conflict there is a real disagreement about the data. Union merge would
# silently duplicate contests instead of making you look.
